# Changelog

## [ 0.9.4 ]
### Changed
- reverted bad ascii encoding error in report fix

## [ 0.9.3 ]
### Changed
- removed deprecated pandas.read_table calls
- fixed bug where R stupidly renames columns
- fixed bug where report generation through ascii encoding errors

## [ 0.9.2 ]
### Added
- added detk-util CLI entry points that were left out in 0.9.1
### Changed
- fixed deseq2 test now that samples as replicates is disabled in
  DESeq2 >v1.22
- fixed incorrect exception type in design matrix column drop

## [ 0.9.1 ]
### Added
- added attention admonition for patsy-lite in de module docs
- fullscreen mode for all plots
- detk-util tidy modules for tidying counts and column data
- standalone report generation
### Changed
- reduced test report counts
- removed DESeq2 require in norm class
- added interactivity to PCA report plots
- fixed but in report shutil.copy path in python 3.5
- reduced precision in JSON output, reducing file output by 80%

## [ 0.9.0 ]
### Added
- modular report functionality
### Changed
- moved version info into module
- updated all CLI docs to have common options
- significant stats module performance improvements
- fixed incorrect ascending/descending text in enrich fgsea CLI
- fixed bug with missing column data in detk-de deseq2

## [ 0.8.2 ]
### Changed
- fixed parse error on underscore in filter
- fixed parse error on period in filter
- changed zeros filter to zero in filter + docs

## [ 0.8.1 ]
### Changed
- fixed bug where fgsea would crash if passed NaN stats

## [ 0.8.0 ]
### Added
- detk-enrich fgsea and tests
### Changed
- fixed incorrect count shrinking
- fixed bug when counts to rlog are not integers
- removed erroneous cli arg print in filter

## [ 0.7.2 ]
### Changed
- CLI bugfix for filter module

## [ 0.7.1 ]
### Changed
- complete overhaul to filter system

## [ 0.7.0 ]
### Changed
- fixed transform CLI bug #42
- enable estimateDispersionsGeneEst functionality when DESeq2 complains about
  dispersions being within two orders of magnitude
- small fixes to CLI docopt usage text
- code refactor and doc changes to outlier module
### Added
- fully implemented vst, rlog, and plog transforms, with tests and docs
- outlier.shrink outlier shrinking method

## [ 0.6.1 ]
### Changed
- fixed bug where patsy lite model term order was different than specified formula
- fixed bug where deseq2 model term order was wrong, causing --last-term-only
  functionality to be incorrect
- fixed issue #37
- addressed issue #39 by changing the default deseq2 behavior to accept raw
  counts by default

## [ 0.6.0 ]
### Added
- tabular output to stats module, in either csv or terminaltables table format
### Changed
- fixed stats pca cli bug
- fixed pct calculation in rowdist and coldist
- refactored stats module into objects for better output control
- better PCA tests

## [ 0.5.1 ]
### Changed
- fix for #35, incorrectly specified stats cli docopt usage
- fix for stats json output bug and tests

## [ 0.5.0 ]
### Added
- norm.fpkm
- norm and de docs page
- de.deseq2
### Changed
- major CLI help overhaul, added individual help messages for norm, de, and stats
- modified entrypoint function signatures to fix cli problems when calling with both detk <cmd> and detk-<cmd> forms
- fixed incorrect JSON output format in stats
- monkeypatched JSON encoding error due to mpld3 NumpyEncoder bug
- many test improvements
- fixed issue #34, allowing some non-alphanumeric characters in patsy_lite formula term names
- switched docs to RTD theme
- workflow docs update

## [ 0.4.0 ]
### Added
- new wrapr interface to replace rpy2
- wrapr tests and docs
- entropy outlier filtering
- t-test differential expression
- preliminary workflow doc
### Changed
- removed all trace of rpy2 hooray

## [ 0.3.4 ]
### Changed
- fixed critical bug in stats entropy function

## [ 0.3.3 ]
### Added
- filter module and docs
- new conda build environment for readthedocs build

## [ 0.3.2 ]
### Changed
- fixed bug in stats.rowzero

## [ 0.3.1 ]
### Added
- PCA to stats model
- more develop stats html output
- preliminary filter nonzero function
### Changed
- fixed deprecated .ix use package wide
- updated setup.py and conda package dependencies

## [ 0.3.0 ]
### Added
- new model description language for de module

## [ 0.2.5 ]
### Changed
- fixed import bug in stats.py

## [ 0.2.4 ]
### Added
- stats module implementation and docs

## [ 0.2.3 ]
### Changed
- fixed issues #3 and #4
- Firth DE attempts to use profile likelihood to estimate confidence intervals
  but falls back to Wald if that fails
- better handling of sample name mismatches between counts and column data
  files

## [ 0.2.2 ]
### Added
- common.py module tests

### Changed
- Added py vs rpy2 deseq2 norm cross check tests
- Reorganized some of the CountMatrix constructor signatures
- Added CountMatrix counts/column name strict checking

## [ 0.2.1 ] - 2017-04-14
### Added
- DESeq2 norm tests and CLI usage bug fix

## [ 0.2.0 ] - 2017-04-12
### Added
- detk-norm deseq2 output option added

## [ 0.1.1 ] - 2017-04-07
### Added
- Firth's logistic regression functionality and tests with CLI output

## [ 0.1 ] - 2017-04-06
### Added
- very limited functionality, what do you want it's the first release
- no CLI output support
- DESeq2 and library size normalization methods and tests implemented
- lots o' stubs
